      "writtenOn": "2021-12-23T08:41:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This scheme means there is a difference between not calling setStaticIpConfiguration and calling it with null ; worse, it means there is no way to reset it to its original state.\n\nI think this is at least very uncustomary. API guidelines section 5.6.5.1, albeit discussing another topic, speaks of using @Nullable setters to reset the properties of the builder.\n\nDo we actually need UNASSIGNED at all ? When reviewing the previous patchset I was thinking that, given that this is a new public API, we may not want to support UNASSIGNED semantics at all ; I was observing that it\u0027s difficult to understand where the old settings will be taken from. At the end of the day a user of this API is looking to configure a network, so API-wise I think it makes more sense to only give them the choice between DHCP or static, without a \"don\u0027t touch what existed\" option, because if they\u0027re looking to configure it they should know what the configuration should be.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 295,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 295,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "02121cbb59cf4fcf3ae7187529376b47644d854e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a00c4784_476794c9",
        "filename": "framework/src/android/net/IpConfiguration.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 295,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-24T01:35:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "+1, the IpAssignment enum does not seem particularly useful. From a public API perspective, I think it\u0027s best to say that IP configuration is either static (in which case the caller must set a non-null StaticIpConfiguration) or dynamic (in which case IP configuration must be null).\n\nI think it\u0027s fine not to support things like \"DHCP but with a manually configured gateway\" or \"DHCP with manually configured DNS servers\". That seems like a marginal use case and one that is difficult to get right (e.g., if the IPv4 address assigned by DHCP is not in the subnet as the gateway).",
      "parentUuid": "1bccf911_b933530e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 295,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 295,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "02121cbb59cf4fcf3ae7187529376b47644d854e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
